emacs NEWS                                               -*- outline -*-

User-visible changes worth mentioning, newest first, after the GNU
Coding Standards (NEWS File). emacs has no releases, so changes are
grouped by year; CHANGELOG.md lists them in detail with commit links.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026

** New features

  Devenv integration: a C-c v menu runs devenv tasks, builds and
  processes, project environments load natively, and devenv-allow and
  devenv-revoke manage auto-activation trust.

  magit-land: the magit status buffer shows the git-land queue (the lane,
  the held and blocked sets, the branches that are not queued), and `&`
  on a set, an item or a branch opens a menu to add, approve, reject,
  remove, retry and bump.

  Daemon service: a Home Manager module runs the Emacs daemon under
  systemd, sets EDITOR and VISUAL to emacsclient, and ships an
  emacsctl command to start, stop and inspect it.

  Git and project workflow: C-x G jumps to files that git status
  reports, the modeline shows uncommitted-change counters, C-x p P
  opens projects with per-project tabs, and C-x p R starts a
  whole-repository review queue.  Jujutsu is supported through vc-jj
  and majutsu.

  Language support: Go, OCaml, Zig, Bazel, Meson, Vue, Astro, QML,
  CUDA, Robot Framework, Structurizr and LikeC4, with Eglot servers,
  formatting on save and tempel snippets wired in.  KDL files get a
  major mode.

  Kotlin: Eglot starts kotlin-lsp or kotlin-language-server, ktfmt
  formats on save, ktlint and detekt report through Flymake, and dape
  debugs through kotlin-debug-adapter.  C-c C-t runs Gradle tests and
  C-c C-z opens a REPL.  All tools come from the project PATH.

  Org notebook and writing tools: Org Babel enables 18 languages with
  a trust-based evaluation prompt, Markdown gets a C-c m command
  prefix, and the verb HTTP client works inside Org buffers.

  Documentation: an Info manual, a generated option and package
  reference, an Emacs Lisp API reference and a project website.

** Changes in behavior

  Emacs 31: the default build is now Emacs 31 and the configuration
  requires 31.1 or newer, adopting the newcomers presets.

  Startup and file opening are much faster: startup drops from
  about ten seconds to about three and find-file from 2.4 s to 0.29 s.

  Completion: popups appear on their own only in code, RET always
  inserts a newline, and TAB indents and then completes.  Setting
  `my-completion-free-tab' restores indent-only TAB.

  Themes: the configuration follows the system appearance and now uses
  the Jylhis light and dark themes, with Geist and Fira Sans fonts.

  Several key bindings moved to avoid shadowing: gptel is on C-c s,
  eca on C-c e, claude-code-ide on C-c q and the git status jump on
  C-x G.

  Terminal and AI defaults: vterm is replaced by ghostel, and gptel
  uses OpenRouter by default, later routing Claude models directly to
  Anthropic.

  Configuration renamed from Jotain to emacs-config, changing the
  Elisp prefix, environment variables and Nix module options.

** Removed features

  macOS support was dropped; the configuration is Linux-only.  The
  wakatime and activity-watch integrations and several menu bar
  entries (mail, news, games) were also removed.

  The nix-on-droid module was removed.

** Bug fixes

  Security hardening: local Elisp trust checks resist directory
  traversal, TLS verifies certificates, editor wrappers protect
  against option injection, and ESLint and Tailwind servers are
  opt-in.

* Noteworthy changes in 2025

** New features

  Nix-packaged distribution: the configuration is installed through a
  Home Manager module, with Nix supplying packages, tree-sitter
  grammars, language servers and fonts, and use-package forms scanned
  automatically.

  Leader key and tools: an M-SPC leader keymap, language modules for
  many languages, a git worktree manager on C-c w, and window split
  toggling on C-x j.

  Integrations: 1Password auth-source, Kitty keyboard protocol support
  in terminals, Corfu kind icons and the gited branch manager.

** Changes in behavior

  The configuration was rewritten into the Jotain distribution of four
  modules requiring Emacs 30.1, and packages now come only from Nix.
